## 2. Bypassing 404 Not Found (Revealing Hidden Files)
Developers often intentionally configure their apps to return a 404 Not Found status code instead of a 403 Forbidden on administrative paths to hide their existence from scanners. [29] 
## Technique A: Null Byte and Extension Spoofing [30] 
If a framework hides a private script page (like config.php), adding termination characters or secondary extension markers can force the server wrapper to locate the binary while ignoring the security routing rule.

* URL Variations to Test:
* https://example.local
   * https://example.local
   * https://example.local.
   * https://example.local (Changing formats)

